course: dictionary
lesson: 14874
title: Reappear: coming back into view
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The start of a word can give you a clue. The part re- means again, so reappear means appear again. To appear is to come into view, so to reappear is to come back into view after you have been gone.
explain: «The cat vanished under the bed, then reappeared at dinnertime.» The cat was there, then it was gone, then it was there again. Ask yourself: did something go away and then come back into view? If yes, the word is reappear.
explain: Words often belong to families. Appear means come into view. Disappear means go out of view. Reappear means come back into view. Learn one word in a family and you can often guess the others.
explain: Reappear is a verb, so its form can change: reappears, reappeared, reappearing. «Each time the eclipse ended, the Moon reappeared in the sky.» Use reappeared for something that came back in the past.
fact: Reappear means to appear again or come back into view after being gone.
fact: The prefix re- means again, as in reheat, rewrite and reappear.
fact: «The missing key reappeared under the sofa.» The key was lost, then it came back into view.
fact: Disappear is the opposite of reappear: it means to go out of view.
fact: In stories, a character or object can reappear, and in science, the Moon reappears after an eclipse.
exercise: «After an hour of rain, the sun reappeared.» What does reappeared mean? | It went away and stayed away | *It came back into view after being gone | It turned into a rainbow | It fell onto the grass
exercise: Which word means go out of view, the opposite of reappear? | appear | shine | *disappear | reappear
exercise: «The rabbit disappeared into the hedge, and later it reappeared by the gate.» Find and copy the word that means came back into view. | *reappeared | hedge | gate | disappeared
test: «The lighthouse lamp went out in the fog, then reappeared at dawn.» What does reappeared mean? | Fell over | *Came back into view | Stayed out of sight | Was painted again
test: Which word fits the gap? The Moon ___ after the eclipse ended. | hopped | rained | disappeared | *reappeared
exam: What does reappear mean? «The magician made the rabbit vanish, then it reappeared in the hat.» | To shrink to nothing | To make a loud noise | *To come back into view after being gone | To be painted again
